# {{ .name }}

A gateway integration for {{ .organization }}: callers `POST` orders to
`{{ .endpointPath }}`, and each one is validated, de-duplicated, transformed to the
canonical `{{ .payloadType }}` contract and published as a `{{ .publishes }}`
CloudEvent.

| Response | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `202 Accepted` | Published; the body carries the event id |
| `200 OK` | Already published (duplicate); nothing sent again |
| `422 Unprocessable Entity` | Rejected by a business rule; raised as a business incident |
| `413 Payload Too Large` | Body over `Gateway:MaxRequestBodyBytes` |
| `503 Service Unavailable` | Try again after `Retry-After` |

The gateway runs via its system host. Build and test it with `task build` and
`task test`; `src/{{ .name }}.http` holds {{ if .empty }}sample requests{{ else }}a sample request for each response{{ end }}.
